# Compose-substitution template ONLY — not a secrets file.
#
# Docker Compose auto-loads a file literally named `.env` in the project root to
# resolve ${VAR} placeholders written directly in compose.yml (volume host paths,
# etc.) — this happens at compose-file-parse time, before any container exists,
# so it is a completely different mechanism from the `env_file:` directive under
# each service (see .env.app.example / .env.db.example, which supply the actual
# per-container secrets and are never read by this substitution step).
#
# Nothing sensitive belongs here. See SECURITY_NOTES.md's "Environment File
# Architecture" section for the full picture.

# ── Docker bind-mount data directory ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host path for postgres/uploads/thumbs bind mounts (see compose.yml). Same path is
# intended to be used on both the VirtualBox VM and the eventual home server.
TELECLOUD_DATA_DIR=/opt/telecloud/data
